  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Engaging Inter-Religious Harmony Forum in Conflict Transformation and Peacebuilding</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">While religious freedom is guaranteed in our Constitution, Indonesia continues to struggle with religious conflicts that harm religious minorities. An increasingly popular strategy in dealing with such conflict is mediation, most notably by the Inter-Religious Harmony Forums (FKUB). Although the use of this non-legal mechanism is perceived to be less costly, less divisive, and more sustainable, mediations by FKUB have been criticized for undermining minority rights. This is because mediation is often misunderstood and misused as a way to &#x201c;legally&#x201d; force the minority to succumb to the majority&#x2019;s demand. The project aims to strengthen local FKUB members and inter-faith leaders by (1) building the mediation skills and knowledge of FKUB members, (2) facilitating them to collaborate with other relevant actors for effective conflict resolution, and (3) developing participatory community processes and forums that can help to build social capital, overcome mistrust, and set a framework for constructive disputes resolution.</narrative>
  </description>
